Now let me also make sure the EHCI driver's `sunxi_isoc_setup` function limits the transfer size to `maxpacket` (not `maxpacket * 8`). Looking at the current code, it already does this:```c
if (buflen > (size_t)epinfo->maxpacket)
  {
    buflen = (size_t)epinfo->maxpacket;
  }
```

This limits each transfer to one maxpacket. With the higher bandwidth alt setting (maxpkt=1024, mult=3), each transfer can be up to 3072 bytes. But the code limits it to maxpacket (1024). 

I'm realizing the multi-transaction handling might be off—if mult=3 means the endpoint supports 3 transactions per micro-frame, then a single transfer should be able to handle up to 3072 bytes, not just the base maxpacket size.

For UVC cameras, each transaction carries one payload with its own header, so the stream thread will call DRVR_TRANSFER repeatedly to fetch each transaction separately. That means limiting to maxpacket per transfer is actually the right approach here.

I should verify that the endpoint descriptor is using the correct maxpacket value from the alt setting.

